## §13 Google Play — Misleading Claims & listing discipline **[core]**

Google reviewers spend **~90–120 seconds** on a cold install. Policy bots also compare **store text + screenshots** to the **in-app experience**. Treat every listing bullet as a testable assertion.

### Canonical source chain (do not break)

```
Web source (HTML/JS/dist)  →  Gradle sync or cap copy  →  AAB  →  Play listing must describe that AAB
```

- Before editing for Android, read the shell’s `build.gradle(.kts)` to learn **which directory** is synced.
- Vendored copies (e.g. embed `public/games/<id>/` on a host site) are **not** the Play bundle unless Gradle points there.
- After web changes: rebuild AAB, install on a **clean** device/emulator, then update listing/screenshots.

### Listing ↔ app matrix (required before every upload)

For **each** bullet in short description, full description, and “What’s new”:

| Question | Must be **Yes** to ship the claim |
|----------|-----------------------------------|
| Does the feature exist in the release AAB? | |
| Can a reviewer find it in **≤120s** without hidden gestures? | |
| Does a store screenshot show it (if non-obvious)? | |
| Is the count exact (levels, themes, modes)? | |

**Derive counts from code/data**, not memory — e.g. `LEVELS.length`, length of `levels.json`, theme array length in JS.

### Wording traps (common rejections)

| Do **not** say | Say instead (if true) |
|----------------|------------------------|
| Multiple **game modes** | Single campaign / puzzle mode; optional: “N visual themes” (skins only — **not** modes) |
| **Leaderboard** / high scores | Only if a **Scores** (or equivalent) control is on the main HUD/menu — label “on this device” if local-only |
| **Hints** | “Help reopens tutorial”, “blocked-path alert”, “undo/reset” — only claim a Hint button if one exists |
| **Online** / multiplayer / cloud save | Only with real network features and `INTERNET` permission + Data safety disclosure |
| Parent brand (e.g. study portal name) on a **standalone** game listing | App name + puzzle identity only; separate privacy policy URL if needed |
| Separate Play apps for **soft-archived** web embeds (Lumen / Orbit / Ghost after flagship merge) | One flagship listing; mention mode in description if needed — do not create/relive archived `applicationId`s |

### Discoverable UI for listed features

If the listing mentions scores, leaderboards, settings, or modes:

1. Add a **primary-toolbar or home-screen** affordance (`title`, `aria-label`, ~48×48dp touch target for icon buttons).
2. Prefer a dedicated overlay/screen — not only game-over or end-of-campaign screens.
3. Empty state is OK (e.g. “No scores yet”) — the **UI chrome** must still be visible.
4. Wire JS through existing modules (e.g. `Leaderboard.load().then(UI.render…)`), not assumed globals.

### All tracks and locales

Play compares metadata across **active release tracks** (Internal, Closed/Open testing, Production) and **all translated listings**.

- Update or **pause** stale tracks before Production submit.
- Check **Custom store listings** and every locale — en-US-only fixes are not enough if hi-IN still has old bullets.

### Standalone app vs portal shell

| Product | Play listing | `applicationId` |
|---------|--------------|-----------------|
| Standalone game (thin WebView) | Game name only; no portal/DSA/LeetCode positioning | May differ from marketing site |
| Full SPA (Capacitor) | Matches app name in `strings.xml` | Consistent with site brand |

Mismatch between icon, title, and first screen is a frequent Misleading Claims flag.

### 120-second reviewer script (run on release AAB)

| Time | Action | Pass |
|------|--------|------|
| 0:00 | Cold install, airplane mode optional | No crash; WebView loads |
| 0:30 | Reach first playable state | Matches screenshot #1 |
| 0:45 | Tap each main-toolbar / home action | All respond visibly |
| 1:00 | Verify **one** listed feature (e.g. themes, scores) | As described in store copy |
| 1:20 | Compare screen to uploaded screenshots | Same layout, theme, buttons |
| 2:00 | Scan logcat for repeated JS errors | None blocking gameplay |

Record screen optional; fix before “Send for review”.

### Resubmission notes (when UI changed)

In Play Console release notes, point reviewers to non-obvious fixes, e.g. *“Local scores: tap the Scores icon in the bottom bar (see screenshot 3).”* Only cite UI that exists in **this** build.

### Safe listing template (puzzle game pattern)

Use as a starting point; **edit counts and features** to match the matrix above:

```text
<AppName> is a <one-line genre>.

• <N> levels — <how progression works>
• Tutorial / onboarding that teaches the rules
• Moves, score, and timer (if shown in HUD)
• Undo, reset, and blocked-state feedback (if implemented)
• <N> visual themes (if theme switcher exists — not “modes”)
• Offline play — no account required (if no network permission)
• Progress saved on this device (if localStorage / local DB)

How to play: <one sentence matching tutorial copy>
```

Omit leaderboard, daily challenge, multiplayer, and “hints” unless §13 matrix passes.

### Policy reference

- [Misleading Claims](https://support.google.com/googleplay/android-developer/answer/9888179) — store listing must match app functionality.
- Rejection for **missing features in description** → fix listing **or** add discoverable UI; appeals rarely succeed without a material change.

