## §15 Android Studio test & Play Store publish **[core]**

End-to-end checklist from **first open in Studio** through **Production** (or Internal testing). Run on **each** game shell before upload.

### A. One-time machine setup

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| JDK | **JDK 17** — `brew install openjdk@17` or use Android Studio’s embedded JDK (Settings → Build → Gradle → Gradle JDK). CLI: `export JAVA_HOME="/opt/homebrew/opt/openjdk@17/libexec/openjdk.jdk/Contents/Home"` |
| Android Studio | Latest stable; install **SDK Platform 35** + **Build-Tools** via SDK Manager |
| Emulator | Device Manager → create phone AVD (e.g. Pixel 7, API 34+) |
| Play Console | [Google Play Console](https://play.google.com/console) — developer account ($25 one-time) |

### B. Build web assets (every web change)

From **game monorepo root** (e.g. Bharat Brawlers):

```bash
node scripts/games/build-android-standalone.mjs <slug>
# slug: circuit-flow | train-panic | grid-tower-defense | pocket-park-tycoon | tank-wars
```

Output: `games/<Name>/dist/android-client/`. Gradle syncs this on next build (§14).

### C. Open project in Android Studio

1. **File → Open** → `games/<Name>/android/` (the folder containing `settings.gradle.kts`, not the repo root).
2. Let Gradle sync finish. If sync fails on JDK 25, set Gradle JDK to **17** in Settings.
3. Confirm `local.properties` exists with `sdk.dir=…` (gitignored; Studio creates it).
4. **Optional CLI sanity check** (faster than Studio for CI):
   ```bash
   cd games/<Name>/android
   ./gradlew :app:assembleDebug
   ```

### D. Run on emulator or device (debug)

1. Start AVD or connect USB device (USB debugging on).
2. Select **app** configuration → **Run** (green play).
3. **Smoke test (offline):** enable airplane mode → force-stop app → cold launch → game home/play loads (no blank WebView).
4. Tap **back** — overlays/routes dismiss before app exits (`GameBack`).
5. Run instrumentation tests (Circuit Flow / Train Panic):
   ```bash
   ./gradlew :app:connectedDebugAndroidTest
   ```
   Or full scripted pass: `node scripts/games/test-android-standalone.mjs` from repo root.

### E. Build signed release AAB

**Do not upload debug APKs to Play.** Use the **production keystore** (back up securely — loss = cannot update the app). Play Store requires **App Bundle (.aab)**, not APK.

#### Production keystore (canonical Play upload key)

